    "updated_at": "2026-01-21T19:37:05Z",
    "body": "Thanks for bringing this up. The reason that the removal steps run cloning is because it may change which selectedcontent becomes the primary one, and we want to keep the primary one up to date. This didn't matter in the original implementation which always updated all selectedcontent elements, but we changed it to only track one \"primary\" selectedcontent element:\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10633#discussion_r1834376985\n- https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/f8190777fa80312a588f06a7b6ba2cf3bd9897a7\n\nIn my opinion, keeping the newly primary selectedcontent element up to date in the case that the primary selectedcontent element is removed is not a use case we should guard against because there is no use case to append multiple selectedcontent elements to a select and then remove the first one, which would be another way to justify removing the selectedcontent element removal steps.\n\nSo I think we have two options to address this issue:\n1. Clone the selected option into every selectedcontent element descendant of the select element instead of the first one in tree order.\n2. Drop the selectedcontent removal steps without any other changes because it guards against a case that isn't important.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
