    "updated_at": "2026-02-15T17:16:49Z",
    "body": "> Updating all `selectedcontent` descendants (that are not disabled) was discussed during [#12087](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12087) and seemed reasonable to everyone present. Let's go with that.\n\nSounds good to me, thanks! I'll get on it.\n\n\n> We currently manage `selectedcontent` disabled state as part of the post-connection steps. This means that if you insert multiple `selectedcontent` elements the first will calculate its disabled state and then trigger the `select` element to find `selectedcontent` element descendants to update. This will end up updating all `selectedcontent` elements descendants, even if they later end up being disabled.\n> \n> So we probably need a new strategy for that too, even if it is an error condition.\n\nAgreed, we should calculate the disabled flag in the insertion steps instead of the post-connection steps.\n\nI'd like to make a PR to do these things, but I already have 3 other PRs open for behavior in this area:\n1. https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11891\n2. https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11890\n3. https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12083\n\nCan we get these merged or should I merge them all into one PR?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
